 listen to the high end. if it sounds muffled, or wrong, or weird, that's because IT IS. generative networks such as the one used to make this song build music out of pure static, isolating certain parts of it to sound louder than others. 

also, generative networks cannot sample like a real artist can. for electronic music, in which case, you'll know instantly, snares and drums are something to listen deeply too. every single hit of a drum sounds different, when electronic drum samples never change how they sound. it's a sample. even then, in normal music, drum samples sound off.
